# Staging pipeline paths, for smoke-testing the chain on a sample drawn from
# the same downloaded data. Use with `make run-staging`.
#
# Every path differs from config/prod.env, so a staging run cannot overwrite
# production's canonical Parquet, its database, or its snapshot registry:
#
#   * a separate registry, because snapshots.py rejects any entry whose status
#     is not `approved` -- there is no way to park an unapproved sample in the
#     real config/snapshots.yaml, so it gets its own file instead;
#   * a separate .duckdb filename, which is its own label: you cannot mistake
#     panchayat-staging.duckdb for the real one in a deploy command;
#   * a separate Parquet tree, so re-normalizing one mode cannot clobber the
#     other's canonical data.
#
# A sample build still cannot be deployed: build_snapshot_manifest.py refuses
# to pin anything short of the full 6,794-GP roster.
PIPELINE_RAW_ROOT=data/raw-staging
PANCHAYAT_CANONICAL_ROOT=data/interim/canonical-staging
PIPELINE_SNAPSHOTS=config/snapshots.staging.yaml
PANCHAYAT_DB_PATH=data/interim/panchayat-staging.duckdb
